1
00:00:01,150 --> 00:00:05,529
Chapter 25 The month of courtship had wasted.

2
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:08,629
Its very last hours were being numbered.

3
00:00:09,529 --> 00:00:14,550
There was no putting off the day that advanced, the bridal day, and all

4
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:16,709
preparations for its arrival were complete.

5
00:00:17,709 --> 00:00:20,290
I at least had nothing more to do.

6
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:24,682
There were my trunks, packed, locked, corded,

7
00:00:24,682 --> 00:00:28,010
ranged in a row along the wall of my little chamber.

8
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:33,989
Tomorrow, at this time, they would be far on their road to London, and so should I,

9
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:40,550
or rather not I, but one Jane Rochester, a person whom as yet I knew not.

10
00:00:41,209 --> 00:00:44,690
The cards of address alone remained to nail on.

11
00:00:45,410 --> 00:00:48,529
They lay four little squares in the drawer.

12
00:00:49,489 --> 00:00:52,169
Mr. Rochester had himself written the direction.

13
00:00:53,209 --> 00:00:57,569
Mrs. Rochester, hotel, London, on each.

14
00:00:58,069 --> 00:01:02,410
I could not persuade myself to affix them, or to have them affixed.

15
00:01:03,169 --> 00:01:06,129
Mrs. Rochester, she did not exist.

16
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:11,250
She would not be born till tomorrow, sometime after 8 o'clock AM.

17
00:01:12,269 --> 00:01:15,366
And I would wait to be assured she had come into the

18
00:01:15,368 --> 00:01:18,309
world alive before I assigned to her all that property.

19
00:01:20,330 --> 00:01:26,889
It was enough that in Yonder Closet opposite my dressing table, Garment said

20
00:01:26,891 --> 00:01:32,870
to be hers had already displaced my black stuff, lowered frock, and straw bonnet.

21
00:01:33,449 --> 00:01:37,250
For not to me, appertained that suit of wedding raiment.

22
00:01:38,069 --> 00:01:43,430
The pearl-coloured robe, the vapory veil pendent from the usurped portmanteau.

23
00:01:43,849 --> 00:01:48,769
I shut the closet to conceal the strange, rath-like apparel it contained,

24
00:01:49,489 --> 00:01:54,713
which, at this evening hour, nine o'clock, gave out certainly

25
00:01:54,714 --> 00:01:57,989
a most ghostly shimmer through the shadow of my apartment.

26
00:01:59,489 --> 00:02:02,910
I will leave you by yourself, white dream, I said.

27
00:02:03,669 --> 00:02:04,989
I am feverish.

28
00:02:05,610 --> 00:02:09,110
I hear the wind blowing, I will go out of doors and feel it.

29
00:02:10,290 --> 00:02:14,110
It was not only the hurry of preparation that made me feverish.

30
00:02:15,129 --> 00:02:18,701
Not only the anticipation of the great change,

31
00:02:18,703 --> 00:02:22,510
the new life which was to commence tomorrow.

32
00:02:22,989 --> 00:02:28,529
Both these circumstances had their share doubtless, in producing that restless,

33
00:02:28,849 --> 00:02:33,389
excited mood which hurried me forth at this late hour into the darkening grounds.

34
00:02:34,330 --> 00:02:38,169
But a third cause influenced my mind more than they.

35
00:02:39,430 --> 00:02:43,309
I had at heart a strange and anxious thought.

36
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:46,650
Something had happened which I did not comprehend.

37
00:02:48,169 --> 00:02:51,069
No one knew of or had seen the event but myself.

38
00:02:52,449 --> 00:02:55,169
It had taken place the preceding night.

39
00:02:56,550 --> 00:03:01,029
Mr. Rochester that night was absent from home, nor was he yet returned.

40
00:03:02,309 --> 00:03:05,790
Business had called him to a smaller state of two or three farms.

41
00:03:06,569 --> 00:03:08,809
He possessed 30 miles off.

42
00:03:09,510 --> 00:03:12,150
Business it was requisite he should settle in person.

43
00:03:13,089 --> 00:03:15,889
Previous to his meditated departure from England.

44
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:22,163
I waited now, his return, eager to disperthen my mind and

45
00:03:22,163 --> 00:03:26,169
to seek of him the solution of the enigma that perplexed me.

46
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:29,169
Stay till he comes, reader.

47
00:03:30,069 --> 00:03:34,589
And when I disclose my secret to him, you shall share the confidence.

48
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:40,213
I sought the orchard, driven to its shelter by the wind,

49
00:03:40,214 --> 00:03:43,989
which all day had blown strong and full from the south.

50
00:03:44,529 --> 00:03:47,730
Without, however, bringing a speck of rain.

51
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:52,025
Instead of subsiding as night drew on, it

52
00:03:52,025 --> 00:03:55,930
seemed to augment its rush and deepen its roar.

53
00:03:56,610 --> 00:04:00,595
The trees blew steadfastly one way, never writhing round

54
00:04:00,597 --> 00:04:04,190
and scarcely tossing back their bows once in an hour.

55
00:04:05,209 --> 00:04:09,089
So continuous was the strain bending their branchy heads northward.

56
00:04:10,089 --> 00:04:15,650
The clouds drifted from pole to pole, fast following, mass on mass.

57
00:04:16,849 --> 00:04:20,010
No glimpse of blue sky had been visible that July day.

58
00:04:21,250 --> 00:04:23,629
It was not without a certain wild pleasure.

59
00:04:24,629 --> 00:04:28,517
I ran before the wind, delivering my trouble of mind to

60
00:04:28,519 --> 00:04:31,470
the measureless air -torrent thundering through space.

61
00:04:32,629 --> 00:04:36,970
Descending the laurel walk, I faced the wreck of the chestnut tree.

62
00:04:37,949 --> 00:04:39,589
It stood up black and driven.

63
00:04:40,470 --> 00:04:44,690
The trunk split down the center, gasped ghastly.

64
00:04:45,809 --> 00:04:48,330
The cloven halves were not broken from each other.

65
00:04:48,949 --> 00:04:53,023
For the firm base and strong roots kept them unsundered

66
00:04:53,023 --> 00:04:56,349
below, though community of vitality was destroyed.

67
00:04:57,449 --> 00:04:59,129
The sap could flow no more.

68
00:04:59,989 --> 00:05:01,970
Their great bows on each side were dead.

69
00:05:02,750 --> 00:05:07,529
And next, winter's tempests would be sure to fell one or both to earth.

70
00:05:08,069 --> 00:05:13,750
As yet, however, they might be said to form one tree, a ruin, but an entire ruin.

71
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:19,438
You did right to hold fast to each other, I said, as if

72
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:22,970
the monster splinters were living things and could hear me.

73
00:05:23,610 --> 00:05:29,889
I think, scathed as you look, and charred and scorched, there must be a little sense

74
00:05:29,891 --> 00:05:35,089
of life in you yet, rising out of that adhesion at the faithful honest roots.

75
00:05:36,250 --> 00:05:38,669
You will never have green leaves more.

76
00:05:39,449 --> 00:05:43,669
Never more see birds making nests and singing idols in your bows.

77
00:05:44,769 --> 00:05:50,169
The time of pleasure and love is over with you, but you are not desolate.

78
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:54,930
Each of you has a comrade to sympathise with him in his decay.

79
00:05:56,830 --> 00:06:00,688
As I looked up at them, the moon appeared momentarily

80
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:03,830
in that part of the sky which filled their fissure.

81
00:06:04,730 --> 00:06:07,389
Her disc was blood red and half overcast.

82
00:06:08,230 --> 00:06:12,074
She seemed to throw on me one bewildered dreary glance and

83
00:06:12,076 --> 00:06:16,069
buried herself again instantly in the deep drift of cloud.

84
00:06:17,050 --> 00:06:22,730
The wind fell for a second round thornfield, but far away over wood and

85
00:06:22,730 --> 00:06:30,671
water poured a wild melancholy whale, it was sad to listen to, and I ran off again.

86
00:06:31,449 --> 00:06:37,309
Here and there, I strayed through the orchard, gathered up the apples with which

87
00:06:37,311 --> 00:06:40,650
the grass around the tree roots was thickly strewn.

88
00:06:41,629 --> 00:06:45,730
Then I employed myself in dividing the ripe from the unripe.

89
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:50,629
I carried them into the house and put them away in the storeroom.

90
00:06:51,370 --> 00:06:55,669
Then I repaired to the library to ascertain whether the fire was lit,

91
00:06:56,290 --> 00:07:01,150
for, though summer, I knew on such a gloomy evening,

92
00:07:01,150 --> 00:07:05,410
Mr. Rochester would like to see a cheerful hearth when he came in.

93
00:07:06,309 --> 00:07:09,809
Yes, the fire had been kindled sometime and burnt well.

94
00:07:10,830 --> 00:07:13,389
I placed his armchair by the chimney corner.

95
00:07:14,069 --> 00:07:18,207
I wheeled the table near it, I let down the curtain,

96
00:07:18,207 --> 00:07:21,510
and had the candles brought in ready for lighting.

97
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:27,841
More restless than ever, when I had completed these arrangements,

98
00:07:27,841 --> 00:07:31,849
I could not sit still, nor even remain in the house.

99
00:07:32,809 --> 00:07:34,930
A little timepiece in the room and the old

100
00:07:34,930 --> 00:07:38,531
clock in the hall simultaneously struck ten.

101
00:07:39,610 --> 00:07:41,669
How late it grows, I said.

102
00:07:42,629 --> 00:07:44,050
I will run down to the gates.

103
00:07:44,889 --> 00:07:46,449
It is moonlight at intervals.

104
00:07:47,309 --> 00:07:48,910
I can see a good way on the road.

105
00:07:49,569 --> 00:07:54,690
He may be coming now, and to meet him will save some minutes of suspense.

106
00:07:56,150 --> 00:08:02,790
The wind roared high in the great trees which emboured the gates, but the road as

107
00:08:02,790 --> 00:08:08,830
far as I could see to the right hand on the left was all still and solitary.

108
00:08:09,669 --> 00:08:13,989
Say for the shadows of clouds crossing it at intervals as the moon looked out,

109
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:19,410
it was but a long pale line unverried by one moving speck.

110
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:23,330
A poor alter dimmed my eye while I looked.

111
00:08:24,309 --> 00:08:28,769
A tear of disappointment and impatience, ashamed of it, I wiped it away.

112
00:08:29,589 --> 00:08:30,589
I lingered.

113
00:08:31,050 --> 00:08:33,764
The moon shut herself wholly within her chamber

114
00:08:33,764 --> 00:08:36,591
and drew close her curtain of dense cloud.

115
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:38,309
The night grew dark.

116
00:08:39,389 --> 00:08:41,430
Rain came driving fast on the gale.

117
00:08:42,389 --> 00:08:43,449
I wish he would come.

118
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:45,209
I wish he would come.

119
00:08:45,709 --> 00:08:48,989
I exclaimed, seized with hyper-condriac foreboding.

120
00:08:49,709 --> 00:08:52,169
I had expected his arrival before tea.

121
00:08:52,930 --> 00:08:53,930
Now it was dark.

122
00:08:54,370 --> 00:08:55,370
What could keep him?

123
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:56,930
Had an accident happened?

124
00:08:57,830 --> 00:09:00,190
The event of last night again recurred to me.

125
00:09:00,930 --> 00:09:03,349
I interpreted it as a warning of disaster.

126
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:06,750
I feared my hopes were too bright to be realised.

127
00:09:07,629 --> 00:09:11,194
And I had enjoyed so much bliss lately, that I imagined

128
00:09:11,194 --> 00:09:15,089
my fortune had passed its meridian and must now decline.

129
00:09:17,529 --> 00:09:20,489
Well, I cannot return to the house, I thought.

130
00:09:21,150 --> 00:09:24,550
I cannot sit by the fireside while he is abroad in inclement weather.

131
00:09:25,309 --> 00:09:27,589
Better tire my limbs than strain my heart.

132
00:09:28,129 --> 00:09:29,449
I will go forward and meet him.

133
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:31,650
I set out.

134
00:09:32,169 --> 00:09:33,809
I walked fast but not far.

135
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,029
Air I had measured a quarter of a mile.

136
00:09:36,629 --> 00:09:37,930
I heard the tramp of hoofs.

137
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:41,730
A horseman came on full gallop, a dog ran by his side.

138
00:09:42,529 --> 00:09:44,349
Away with evil presentiment.

139
00:09:45,029 --> 00:09:46,029
It was he.

140
00:09:46,190 --> 00:09:49,629
Here he was, mounted on Mezruhr, followed by pilot.

141
00:09:50,449 --> 00:09:51,449
He saw me.

142
00:09:52,029 --> 00:09:57,089
For the moon had opened a blue field in the sky and rode in it watery bright.

143
00:09:57,769 --> 00:10:00,769
He took his hat off and waved it round his head.

144
00:10:01,449 --> 00:10:02,949
I now ran to meet him.

145
00:10:03,690 --> 00:10:08,830
There, he exclaimed, as he stretched out his hand and bent from the saddle.

146
00:10:09,870 --> 00:10:12,129
You can't do without me, that is evident.

147
00:10:13,010 --> 00:10:16,050
Step on my boot toe, give me both hands, mount.

148
00:10:17,410 --> 00:10:18,529
I obeyed.

149
00:10:19,129 --> 00:10:20,449
Joy made me agile.

150
00:10:21,250 --> 00:10:22,569
I sprang up before him.

151
00:10:23,449 --> 00:10:26,271
A hearty kissing I got for a welcome, and some

152
00:10:26,273 --> 00:10:29,069
boastful triumph, which I swallowed as well as I could.

153
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:36,849
He checked himself in his exaltation to demand, but is there anything the matter,

154
00:10:37,069 --> 00:10:39,930
Janet, that you come to meet me at such an hour?

155
00:10:40,750 --> 00:10:41,750
Is there anything wrong?

156
00:10:43,529 --> 00:10:46,269
No, but I thought you would never come.

157
00:10:47,190 --> 00:10:52,029
I could not bear to wait in the house for you, especially with this rain and wind.

158
00:10:53,010 --> 00:10:56,949
Rain and wind indeed, yes, you are dripping like a mermaid.

159
00:10:57,769 --> 00:11:01,188
Pull my cloak round you, but I think you are feverish,

160
00:11:01,190 --> 00:11:04,269
Jane, both your cheek and hand are burning hot.

161
00:11:05,690 --> 00:11:08,449
I ask again, is there anything the matter?

162
00:11:09,830 --> 00:11:10,830
Nothing now.

163
00:11:11,489 --> 00:11:13,209
I am neither afraid nor unhappy.

164
00:11:14,290 --> 00:11:15,330
Then you have been both?

165
00:11:17,269 --> 00:11:20,703
Rather, but I'll tell you all about it by and by, sir,

166
00:11:20,703 --> 00:11:24,050
and I dare say you will only laugh at me for my pains.

167
00:11:25,389 --> 00:11:29,790
I'll laugh at you heartily when tomorrow is past, till then I dare not.

168
00:11:30,370 --> 00:11:31,709
My prize is not certain.

169
00:11:32,449 --> 00:11:35,536
This is you, who have been as slippery as an eel

170
00:11:35,538 --> 00:11:39,031
this last month, and as thorny as a briarose.

171
00:11:39,589 --> 00:11:43,383
I could not lay a finger anywhere but I was pricked, and

172
00:11:43,383 --> 00:11:46,410
now I seem to have gathered up a stray lamb in my arms.

173
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:50,370
You wandered out of the fold to seek your shepherd, did you, Jane?

174
00:11:51,529 --> 00:11:54,290
I wanted you, but don't boast.

175
00:11:55,050 --> 00:11:56,349
Here we are at Thornfield.

176
00:11:56,849 --> 00:11:57,930
Now, let me get down.

177
00:11:59,370 --> 00:12:00,809
He landed me on the pavement.

178
00:12:02,089 --> 00:12:06,150
As John took his horse, and he followed me into the hall.

179
00:12:06,949 --> 00:12:10,370
He told me to make haste and put something dry on, and

180
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:13,849
then returned to him in the library, and he stopped me.

181
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:20,110
As I made for the staircase, to extort a promise that I would not be long.

182
00:12:21,129 --> 00:12:22,169
Nor was I long.

183
00:12:23,230 --> 00:12:25,150
In five minutes I rejoined him.

184
00:12:25,470 --> 00:12:26,949
I found him at supper.

185
00:12:28,410 --> 00:12:30,930
Take a seat and bear me company, Jane.

186
00:12:31,790 --> 00:12:34,101
Please, God, it is the last meal, but one you

187
00:12:34,101 --> 00:12:36,889
will eat at Thornfield Hall for a long time.

188
00:12:37,930 --> 00:12:41,569
I sat down near him, but told him I could not eat.

189
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:46,830
Is it because you have the prospect of a journey before you, Jane?

190
00:12:47,970 --> 00:12:51,269
Is it the thoughts of going to London that takes away your appetite?

191
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:56,326
I cannot see my prospects clearly tonight, sir,

192
00:12:56,326 --> 00:12:59,790
and I hardly know what thoughts I have in my head.

193
00:13:00,629 --> 00:13:02,690
Everything in life seems unreal.

194
00:13:04,290 --> 00:13:05,290
Accept me.

195
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:07,230
I am substantial enough.

196
00:13:08,029 --> 00:13:09,029
Touch me.

197
00:13:09,889 --> 00:13:12,610
You, sir, are the most phantom like of all.

198
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:14,550
You are a mere dream.

199
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:17,309
He held out his hand, laughing.

200
00:13:18,529 --> 00:13:19,529
Is that a dream?

201
00:13:19,930 --> 00:13:21,889
Said he, placing it close to my eyes.

202
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:27,230
He had a rounded muscular and vigorous hand as well as a long strong arm.

203
00:13:28,449 --> 00:13:34,711
Yes, though I touch it, it is a dream, said I, as I put it down from before my face.

204
00:13:34,989 --> 00:13:37,050
Sir, have you finished supper?

205
00:13:38,349 --> 00:13:39,349
Yes, Jane.

206
00:13:40,269 --> 00:13:42,250
I rang the bell and ordered away the tray.

207
00:13:43,370 --> 00:13:45,989
When we were again alone, I stirred the fire,

208
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,830
and then took a low seat at my master's knee.

209
00:13:49,209 --> 00:13:51,510
It is near midnight, I said.

210
00:13:52,430 --> 00:13:57,389
Yes, but remember, Jane, you promised to wake with me the night before my wedding.

211
00:13:58,430 --> 00:14:03,129
I did, and I will keep my promise for an hour or two at least.

212
00:14:03,970 --> 00:14:05,870
I have no wish to go to bed.

213
00:14:07,050 --> 00:14:08,629
Are all your arrangements complete?

214
00:14:09,910 --> 00:14:13,849
Also, and on my part likewise, he returned.

215
00:14:14,610 --> 00:14:18,392
I have settled everything, and we shall leave Thornfield

216
00:14:18,394 --> 00:14:21,430
tomorrow, within half an hour after our return from church.

217
00:14:22,650 --> 00:14:23,650
Very well, sir.

218
00:14:24,449 --> 00:14:26,930
With what an extraordinary smile you uttered that word?

219
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:29,309
Very well, Jane.

220
00:14:30,190 --> 00:14:32,489
What a bright spot of colour you have on each

221
00:14:32,491 --> 00:14:35,591
cheek, and how strangely your eyes glitter.

222
00:14:35,669 --> 00:14:36,669
Are you well?

223
00:14:37,269 --> 00:14:38,389
I believe I am.

224
00:14:39,290 --> 00:14:40,290
Believe.

225
00:14:40,410 --> 00:14:40,970
What is the matter?

226
00:14:41,209 --> 00:14:42,209
Tell me what you feel.

227
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:44,389
I could not, sir.

228
00:14:45,290 --> 00:14:47,269
No words could tell you what I feel.

229
00:14:48,330 --> 00:14:50,589
I wish this present hour would never end.

230
00:14:51,309 --> 00:14:54,610
Who knows, with what fate the next may come charged?

231
00:14:55,290 --> 00:14:56,830
This is hyper-condria, Jane.

232
00:14:57,830 --> 00:15:00,669
You have been over-excited or over -fateaked.

233
00:15:01,750 --> 00:15:04,290
Do you, sir, feel calm and happy?

234
00:15:05,209 --> 00:15:08,349
Calm, no, but happy, to the heart's core.

235
00:15:09,830 --> 00:15:12,290
I looked up at him to read the signs of bliss in his face.

236
00:15:13,069 --> 00:15:14,629
It was ardent and flushed.

237
00:15:15,930 --> 00:15:19,089
Give me your confidence, Jane, he said.

238
00:15:19,889 --> 00:15:24,230
Relieve your mind of any weight that oppresses it by imparting it to me.

239
00:15:24,669 --> 00:15:28,309
What do you fear that I shall not prove a good husband?

240
00:15:29,529 --> 00:15:32,110
It is the idea farthest from my thoughts.

241
00:15:33,430 --> 00:15:36,588
Are you apprehensive of the new sphere you are about

242
00:15:36,588 --> 00:15:39,230
to enter of the new life into which you are passing?

243
00:15:40,370 --> 00:15:41,370
No.

244
00:15:41,910 --> 00:15:43,050
You puzzle me, Jane.

245
00:15:43,529 --> 00:15:47,029
Your look and tone of sorrowful audacity perplex and pain me.

246
00:15:47,910 --> 00:15:48,910
I want an explanation.

247
00:15:49,989 --> 00:15:51,209
Then, sir, listen.

248
00:15:52,169 --> 00:15:53,430
You were from home last night?

249
00:15:54,849 --> 00:15:55,849
I was.

250
00:15:56,129 --> 00:15:57,129
I know that.

251
00:15:57,650 --> 00:16:00,529
And you hinted a while ago at something which had happened in my absence.

252
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:03,010
Nothing, probably, of consequence.

253
00:16:03,769 --> 00:16:06,470
But, in short, it has disturbed you.

254
00:16:06,949 --> 00:16:07,949
Let me hear it.

255
00:16:08,830 --> 00:16:11,069
Mrs. Fairfax has said something, perhaps.

256
00:16:11,989 --> 00:16:14,129
Or, you have overheard the servants talk.

257
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:17,449
Your sensitive self-respect has been wounded?

258
00:16:18,870 --> 00:16:19,870
No, sir.

259
00:16:20,949 --> 00:16:21,989
It struck twelve.

260
00:16:22,870 --> 00:16:26,211
I waited till the time piece had concluded its silver

261
00:16:26,211 --> 00:16:29,529
chime and the clock its horse vibrating stroke.

262
00:16:30,529 --> 00:16:31,529
And then I proceeded.

263
00:16:32,910 --> 00:16:38,250
All day yesterday I was very busy and very happy in my ceaseless bustle.

264
00:16:38,730 --> 00:16:42,063
For I am not, as you seem to think, troubled by

265
00:16:42,063 --> 00:16:45,949
any haunting fears about the new sphere, etc.

266
00:16:47,290 --> 00:16:52,851
I think it a glorious thing to have the hope of living with you because I love you.

267
00:16:53,089 --> 00:16:54,089
No, sir.

268
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:55,430
Don't caress me now.

269
00:16:56,430 --> 00:16:57,930
Let me talk undisturbed.

270
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:02,968
Yesterday, I trusted well in providence and believed

271
00:17:02,968 --> 00:17:06,529
that events were working together for your good and mine.

272
00:17:07,910 --> 00:17:09,589
It was a fine day.

273
00:17:10,290 --> 00:17:14,425
If you recollect the calmness of the air and sky forbade

274
00:17:14,427 --> 00:17:18,410
apprehensions respecting your safety or comfort on your journey.

275
00:17:19,110 --> 00:17:23,410
I walked a little while on the pavement after tea, thinking of you.

276
00:17:24,449 --> 00:17:31,171
And I beheld you in imagination so near me, I scarcely missed your actual presence.

277
00:17:31,730 --> 00:17:33,790
I thought of the life that lay before me.

278
00:17:34,669 --> 00:17:39,449
Your life, sir, an existence more expansive and stirring than my own.

279
00:17:40,290 --> 00:17:44,427
As much more so, as the depths of the sea to which the Brook

280
00:17:44,427 --> 00:17:48,110
Runs are than the shallows of its own straight channel.

281
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:52,769
I wondered why moralists call this world a dreary wilderness.

282
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:56,209
For me, it blossomed like a rose.

283
00:17:57,209 --> 00:18:01,449
Just at sunset, the air turned cold and the sky cloudy.

284
00:18:02,569 --> 00:18:03,569
I went in.

285
00:18:04,349 --> 00:18:08,591
Sophie called me upstairs to look at my wedding dress, which they had just brought.

286
00:18:08,970 --> 00:18:11,970
And under it, in the box, I found your present.

287
00:18:13,169 --> 00:18:17,790
The veil, which in your princely extravagance you sent for from London.

288
00:18:18,949 --> 00:18:22,627
Resolved, I suppose, since I would not have jewels

289
00:18:22,627 --> 00:18:25,709
to cheat me into accepting something as costly.

290
00:18:26,629 --> 00:18:34,150
I smiled as I unfolded it and devised how I would tease you about your aristocratic

291
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:40,690
tastes and your efforts to mask your plebeian bride in the attributes of a pierce.

292
00:18:40,690 --> 00:18:46,889
I thought how I would carry down to you the square of unembroidered blonde.

293
00:18:47,849 --> 00:18:53,110
I had myself prepared as a covering for my low-born head, and asked if that was not

294
00:18:53,110 --> 00:18:57,790
good enough for a woman who could bring her husband, neither fortune, beauty,

295
00:18:58,129 --> 00:18:59,129
nor connections.

296
00:19:00,150 --> 00:19:07,089
I saw plainly how you would look and heard your impetuous republican answers and your

297
00:19:07,091 --> 00:19:13,010
haughty disavowal of any necessity on your part to augment your wealth or elevate

298
00:19:13,010 --> 00:19:17,550
your standing by marrying either a purse or a coronet.

299
00:19:19,849 --> 00:19:24,510
How well you read me, you witch, interposed Mr. Rochester.

300
00:19:25,209 --> 00:19:28,269
But what did you find in the veil besides its embroidery?

301
00:19:29,069 --> 00:19:32,769
Did you find poison or a dagger that you look so mournful now?

302
00:19:34,489 --> 00:19:35,730
No, no, sir.

303
00:19:36,330 --> 00:19:42,209
Besides the delicacy and richness of the fabric, I found nothing save Fairfax

304
00:19:42,211 --> 00:19:45,142
Rochester's pride, and that did not scare me

305
00:19:45,144 --> 00:19:47,769
because I am used to the sight of the demon.

306
00:19:48,510 --> 00:19:51,830
But, sir, as it grew dark, the wind rose.

307
00:19:52,730 --> 00:19:57,237
It blew yesterday evening, not as it blows now, wild and

308
00:19:57,237 --> 00:20:01,750
high, but with a sullen moaning sound, far more eerie.

309
00:20:03,029 --> 00:20:04,470
I wished you were at home.

310
00:20:05,629 --> 00:20:10,891
I came into this room, and the sight of the empty chair and fireless hearth chilled me.

311
00:20:11,610 --> 00:20:14,709
For some time after I went to bed, I could not sleep.

312
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:19,050
A sense of anxious excitement distressed me.

313
00:20:20,209 --> 00:20:24,489
The gale still rising seemed to my ear to muffle a mournful under sound.

314
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:29,790
Whether in the house or abroad I could not at first tell, but it recurred,

315
00:20:30,110 --> 00:20:32,889
doubtful yet doleful at every lull.

316
00:20:33,629 --> 00:20:37,190
At last I made out it must be some dog howling at a distance.

317
00:20:37,970 --> 00:20:39,330
I was glad when it ceased.

318
00:20:40,569 --> 00:20:45,349
On sleeping I continued in dreams the idea of a dark and gusty night.

319
00:20:46,589 --> 00:20:50,733
I continued also the wish to be with you, and experienced a

320
00:20:50,735 --> 00:20:55,169
strange regretful consciousness of some barrier dividing us.

321
00:20:55,849 --> 00:21:01,309
During all my first sleep I was following the windings of an unknown road.

322
00:21:01,910 --> 00:21:06,129
Total obscurity environment me, rain pelted me.

323
00:21:06,610 --> 00:21:12,690
I was burdened with the charge of a little child, a very small creature, too young

324
00:21:12,690 --> 00:21:15,997
and feeble to walk, and which shivered in my

325
00:21:15,997 --> 00:21:20,271
cold arms, and wailed piteously in my ear.

326
00:21:20,330 --> 00:21:26,730
I thought, sir, that you were on the road a long way before me, and I strained every

327
00:21:26,730 --> 00:21:32,489
nerve to overtake you, and made effort on effort to utter your name and in treat you

328
00:21:32,491 --> 00:21:38,830
to stop, but my movements were fettered, and my voice still died away in

329
00:21:38,830 --> 00:21:45,129
articulate, while you, I felt, withdrew farther and farther every moment.

330
00:21:46,069 --> 00:21:50,529
And these dreams weigh on your spirits now, Jane, when I am close to you?

331
00:21:51,389 --> 00:21:56,669
Little nervous subject, forget visionary woe, and think only of real happiness.

332
00:21:57,330 --> 00:22:02,891
You say you love me Janet, yes, I will not forget that, and you cannot deny it.

333
00:22:03,870 --> 00:22:07,430
Those words did not die in articulate on your lips.

334
00:22:08,129 --> 00:22:13,510
I heard them clear and soft, a thought too solemn perhaps, but sweet as music.

335
00:22:14,610 --> 00:22:18,250
I think it is a glorious thing to have the hope of living with you, Edward,

336
00:22:18,470 --> 00:22:19,470
because I love you.

337
00:22:21,050 --> 00:22:22,129
Do you love me, Jane?

338
00:22:22,730 --> 00:22:23,150
Repeat it.

339
00:22:23,730 --> 00:22:26,250
I do, sir, I do with my whole heart.

340
00:22:27,269 --> 00:22:32,296
Well, he said, after some minutes silence, it is strange,

341
00:22:32,296 --> 00:22:35,589
but that sentence has penetrated my breast painfully.

342
00:22:36,050 --> 00:22:37,050
Why?

343
00:22:37,389 --> 00:22:42,250
I think because you said it with such an earnest, religious energy, and because

344
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:46,870
your upward gaze at me now is the very sublime of faith, truth, and devotion.

345
00:22:47,389 --> 00:22:51,029
It is too much, as if some spirit were near me.

346
00:22:53,389 --> 00:22:57,182
Look wicked, Jane, as you know well how to look,

347
00:22:57,184 --> 00:23:01,211
coin one of your wild shy provoking smiles.

348
00:23:01,470 --> 00:23:02,709
Tell me you hate me.

349
00:23:03,410 --> 00:23:04,550
Tease me, vex me.

350
00:23:05,250 --> 00:23:06,629
Do anything but move me.

351
00:23:07,389 --> 00:23:10,110
I would rather be incensed than saddened.

352
00:23:11,529 --> 00:23:17,230
I will tease you and vex you to your heart's content when I have finished my tale.

353
00:23:17,529 --> 00:23:18,790
But hear me to the end.

354
00:23:20,209 --> 00:23:22,250
I thought, Jane, you had told me all.

355
00:23:23,110 --> 00:23:25,830
I thought I had found the source of your melancholy in a dream.

356
00:23:26,610 --> 00:23:27,610
I shook my head.

357
00:23:28,269 --> 00:23:28,550
What?

358
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:30,150
Is there more?

359
00:23:30,830 --> 00:23:33,110
But I will not believe it to be anything important.

360
00:23:34,029 --> 00:23:36,050
I warn you of incredulity beforehand.

361
00:23:36,930 --> 00:23:37,930
Go on.

362
00:23:39,209 --> 00:23:43,970
The disquietude of his air, the somewhat apprehensive impatience of his manner,

363
00:23:44,629 --> 00:23:46,129
surprised me, but I proceeded.

364
00:23:47,410 --> 00:23:52,430
I dreamt another dream, sir, that Thornfield Hall was a dreary ruin,

365
00:23:53,389 --> 00:23:55,470
the retreat of bats and owls.

366
00:23:56,330 --> 00:24:00,730
I thought that of all the stately front nothing remained but a shell like wall,

367
00:24:01,569 --> 00:24:03,650
very high and very fragile looking.

368
00:24:04,489 --> 00:24:09,849
I wandered on a moonlight night through the grass-grown enclosure within.

369
00:24:11,370 --> 00:24:16,889
Here I stumbled over a marble hearth and there over a fallen fragment of corners.

370
00:24:18,309 --> 00:24:23,050
Rapped up in a shawl, I still carried the unknown little child.

371
00:24:23,769 --> 00:24:25,809
I might not lay it down anywhere.

372
00:24:26,510 --> 00:24:30,809
However tired were my arms, however much its weight impeded my progress,

373
00:24:31,489 --> 00:24:32,730
I must retain it.

374
00:24:33,790 --> 00:24:36,750
I heard the gallop of a horse at a distance on the road.

375
00:24:37,550 --> 00:24:40,449
I was sure it was you, and you were departing

376
00:24:40,451 --> 00:24:43,790
for many years and for a distant country.

377
00:24:43,970 --> 00:24:47,849
I climbed the thin wall with frantic perilous haste,

378
00:24:47,851 --> 00:24:50,631
eager to catch one glimpse of you from the top.

379
00:24:51,389 --> 00:24:56,730
The stones rolled from under my feet, the ivy branches I grasped gave way.

380
00:24:57,330 --> 00:25:01,870
The child clung round my neck in terror and almost strangled me.

381
00:25:02,410 --> 00:25:04,230
At last I gained the summit.

382
00:25:05,190 --> 00:25:09,050
I saw you like a speck on a white track, lessening every moment.

383
00:25:10,050 --> 00:25:13,169
The blast blew so strong I could not stand.

384
00:25:14,150 --> 00:25:15,669
I sat down on the narrow ledge.

385
00:25:16,529 --> 00:25:18,370
I hushed the scared infant in my lap.

386
00:25:19,150 --> 00:25:20,470
You turned an angle of the road.

387
00:25:21,110 --> 00:25:22,889
I bent forward to take a last look.

388
00:25:23,610 --> 00:25:24,610
The wall crumbled.

389
00:25:25,069 --> 00:25:26,069
I was shaken.

390
00:25:26,209 --> 00:25:27,569
The child rolled from my knee.

391
00:25:27,709 --> 00:25:29,610
I lost my balance fell and woke.

392
00:25:30,209 --> 00:25:33,510
Now, Jane, that is all.

393
00:25:34,849 --> 00:25:38,150
All the preface, sir, the tale is yet to come.

394
00:25:39,209 --> 00:25:42,370
On waking, a gleam dazzled my eyes.

395
00:25:42,949 --> 00:25:47,690
I thought, oh, it is daylight, but I was mistaken.

396
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:49,709
It was only candlelight.

397
00:25:50,550 --> 00:25:52,430
Sophie, I supposed, had come in.

398
00:25:53,150 --> 00:25:57,529
There was a light in the dressing table and the door of the closet, where before

399
00:25:57,531 --> 00:26:01,870
going to bed, I had hung my wedding dress and veil, stood open.

400
00:26:02,690 --> 00:26:03,849
I heard a rustling there.

401
00:26:04,449 --> 00:26:08,010
I asked, Sophie, what are you doing?

402
00:26:09,489 --> 00:26:13,089
No one answered, but a form emerged from the closet.

403
00:26:13,870 --> 00:26:16,415
It took the light, held it aloft, and surveyed

404
00:26:16,415 --> 00:26:18,911
the garment's pendant from the portmanteau.

405
00:26:20,790 --> 00:26:26,690
Sophie, Sophie, I again cried, and still it was silent.

406
00:26:27,610 --> 00:26:28,870
I had risen up in bed.

407
00:26:29,349 --> 00:26:30,349
I bent forward.

408
00:26:30,529 --> 00:26:33,796
First surprise, then bewilderment came over me,

409
00:26:33,796 --> 00:26:36,671
and then my blood crept cold through my veins.

410
00:26:37,889 --> 00:26:41,951
Mr. Rochester, this was not Sophie, it was not Leah, it was not Mrs.

411
00:26:42,171 --> 00:26:47,190
Fairfax, it was not... No, I was sure of it, and am still.

412
00:26:48,110 --> 00:26:51,430
It was not even that strange woman, Grace Pool.

413
00:26:52,650 --> 00:26:56,190
It must have been one of them, interrupted my master.

414
00:26:57,089 --> 00:26:59,889
No, sir, I solemnly assure you to the contrary.

415
00:27:00,470 --> 00:27:03,411
The shape standing before me had never crossed my

416
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:06,430
eyes within the precincts of Thornfield Hall before.

417
00:27:07,069 --> 00:27:09,690
The height, the contour were new to me.

418
00:27:11,029 --> 00:27:12,029
Describe it, Jane.

419
00:27:12,970 --> 00:27:16,046
It seemed sir a woman tall and large, with

420
00:27:16,048 --> 00:27:19,970
thick and dark hair hanging long down her back.

421
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:22,150
I know not what dress she had on.

422
00:27:22,809 --> 00:27:23,949
It was white and straight.

423
00:27:24,849 --> 00:27:27,669
But whether gown, sheet, or shroud, I cannot tell.

424
00:27:28,809 --> 00:27:29,849
Did you see her face?

425
00:27:30,949 --> 00:27:35,650
Not at first, but presently she took my veil from its place.

426
00:27:36,449 --> 00:27:42,589
She held it up, gazed at it long, and then she threw it over her own head,

427
00:27:43,129 --> 00:27:44,410
and turned to the mirror.

428
00:27:45,190 --> 00:27:48,480
At that moment I saw the reflection of the visage and

429
00:27:48,482 --> 00:27:51,949
features quite distinctly in the dark oblong glass.

430
00:27:52,970 --> 00:27:54,269
And how were they?

431
00:27:55,510 --> 00:27:57,330
Fearful and ghastly to me.

432
00:27:57,830 --> 00:28:00,529
Oh, sir, I never saw a face like it.

433
00:28:01,150 --> 00:28:02,510
It was a discolored face.

434
00:28:03,230 --> 00:28:04,709
It was a savage face.

435
00:28:05,510 --> 00:28:08,105
I wish I could forget the role of the red eyes and

436
00:28:08,107 --> 00:28:10,750
the fearful blackened inflation of the lineaments.

437
00:28:12,309 --> 00:28:14,250
Ghosts are usually pale, Jane.

438
00:28:15,430 --> 00:28:17,169
This, sir, was purple.

439
00:28:17,949 --> 00:28:19,629
The lips were swelled and dark.

440
00:28:20,389 --> 00:28:21,610
The brow furrowed.

441
00:28:22,150 --> 00:28:25,190
The black eye brows widely raised over the bloodshot eyes.

442
00:28:25,910 --> 00:28:27,569
Shall I tell you of what it reminded me?

443
00:28:28,930 --> 00:28:29,930
You may.

444
00:28:30,889 --> 00:28:33,430
Of the foul German specter, the vampire.

445
00:28:34,529 --> 00:28:36,029
Ah, what did it do?

446
00:28:37,010 --> 00:28:41,273
Sir, it removed my veil from its gaunt head, rented it in

447
00:28:41,273 --> 00:28:44,470
two parts, and flinging both on the floor trampled on them.

448
00:28:45,489 --> 00:28:50,430
Afterwards, it drew aside the window curtain and looked out.

449
00:28:51,269 --> 00:28:52,949
Perhaps it saw a dawn approaching.

450
00:28:53,569 --> 00:28:56,769
For, taking the candle, it retreated to the door.

451
00:28:57,790 --> 00:29:00,089
Just at my bedside, the figure stopped.

452
00:29:00,930 --> 00:29:03,290
The fiery eyes glared upon me.

453
00:29:04,069 --> 00:29:09,069
She thrust up her candle close to my face and extinguished it under my eyes.

454
00:29:10,089 --> 00:29:15,150
I was aware her lurid visage flamed over mine, and I lost consciousness.

455
00:29:16,050 --> 00:29:19,110
For the second time in my life, only the second time.

456
00:29:19,910 --> 00:29:22,470
I became insensible from terror.

457
00:29:23,949 --> 00:29:25,370
Who was with you when you revived?

458
00:29:26,470 --> 00:29:28,529
No one, sir, but the broad day.

459
00:29:29,349 --> 00:29:35,589
I rose, bathed my head and face in water, drank a long draft, felt that though

460
00:29:35,591 --> 00:29:38,610
enfeebled, I was not ill, and determined that

461
00:29:38,610 --> 00:29:42,290
to none but you would I impart this vision.

462
00:29:42,629 --> 00:29:46,849
Now, sir, tell me who and what that woman was.

463
00:29:47,470 --> 00:29:50,370
The creature of an overstimulated brain.

464
00:29:50,949 --> 00:29:52,209
That is certain.

465
00:29:53,029 --> 00:29:54,750
I must be careful of you, my treasure.

466
00:29:55,750 --> 00:29:58,889
Nerves like yours were not made for rough handling.

467
00:30:00,550 --> 00:30:02,129
Sir, depend on it.

468
00:30:02,709 --> 00:30:04,290
My nerves were not in fault.

469
00:30:05,029 --> 00:30:06,029
The thing was real.

470
00:30:06,330 --> 00:30:08,110
The transaction actually took place.

471
00:30:09,069 --> 00:30:11,889
And your previous dreams, were they real, too?

472
00:30:12,629 --> 00:30:14,470
Is Thornfield Hall a ruin?

473
00:30:15,190 --> 00:30:17,750
Am I severed from you by insuperable obstacles?

474
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:22,410
Am I leaving you without a tear, without a kiss, without a word?

475
00:30:23,489 --> 00:30:24,489
Not yet.

476
00:30:25,349 --> 00:30:27,069
Am I about to do it?

477
00:30:27,989 --> 00:30:32,569
Why, the day is already commenced, which is to bind us into solubly.

478
00:30:33,129 --> 00:30:38,190
And when we are once united, there shall be no recurrence of these mental terrors.

479
00:30:38,690 --> 00:30:39,730
I guarantee that.

480
00:30:41,669 --> 00:30:45,809
Mental terrors, sir, I wish I could believe them to be only such.

481
00:30:46,389 --> 00:30:49,470
I wish it more now than ever, since even you cannot

482
00:30:49,472 --> 00:30:52,790
explain to me the mystery of that awful visitant.

483
00:30:53,930 --> 00:30:58,470
And since I cannot do it, Jane, it must have been unreal.

484
00:30:59,790 --> 00:31:05,849
But, sir, when I said so to myself on rising this morning, and when I looked

485
00:31:05,851 --> 00:31:10,470
around the room to gather courage and comfort, from the cheerful aspect of each

486
00:31:10,470 --> 00:31:15,252
familiar object in full daylight, there, on the carpet,

487
00:31:15,254 --> 00:31:18,589
I saw what gave the distinct lie to my hypothesis.

488
00:31:19,449 --> 00:31:23,489
The veil torn from top to bottom in two halves.

489
00:31:24,750 --> 00:31:27,209
I felt Mr. Rochester start and shudder.

490
00:31:27,870 --> 00:31:29,750
He hastily flung his arms around me.

491
00:31:30,449 --> 00:31:36,589
Thank God, he exclaimed, that if anything malignant did come near you last night,

492
00:31:37,129 --> 00:31:39,029
it was only the veil that was harmed.

493
00:31:40,150 --> 00:31:42,410
Oh, to think what might have happened.

494
00:31:43,370 --> 00:31:49,309
He drew his breath short and strained me so close to him I could scarcely pant.

495
00:31:50,150 --> 00:31:54,029
After some minute silence, he continued cheerily.

496
00:31:55,470 --> 00:31:59,010
Now, Janet, I'll explain to you all about it.

497
00:31:59,730 --> 00:32:01,949
It was half-dream, half-reality.

498
00:32:02,709 --> 00:32:05,783
A woman did, I doubt not, enter your room,

499
00:32:05,785 --> 00:32:10,110
and that woman was must have been grace pool.

500
00:32:10,389 --> 00:32:12,730
You call her a strange being yourself.

501
00:32:13,309 --> 00:32:17,330
From all you know, you have reason so to call her, what did she do to me?

502
00:32:17,529 --> 00:32:18,529
What to Mason?

503
00:32:20,290 --> 00:32:25,989
In a state between sleeping and waking, you noticed her entrance and her actions,

504
00:32:26,989 --> 00:32:30,190
but feverish, almost delirious as you were.

505
00:32:30,870 --> 00:32:34,910
You ascribed to her, a goblin appearance different from her own.

506
00:32:35,730 --> 00:32:40,910
The long, dishevelled hair, the swelled black face, the exaggerated stature,

507
00:32:41,430 --> 00:32:45,572
were figments of imagination, results of nightmare, the

508
00:32:45,572 --> 00:32:49,470
spiteful tearing of the veil was real, and it is like her.

509
00:32:51,569 --> 00:32:56,470
I see you would ask why I keep such a woman in my house, when we have been

510
00:32:56,470 --> 00:33:00,169
married a year and a day I will tell you, but not now.

511
00:33:01,050 --> 00:33:02,129
Are you satisfied, Jane?

512
00:33:02,131 --> 00:33:04,470
Do you accept my solution of the mystery?

513
00:33:05,510 --> 00:33:06,569
I reflected.

514
00:33:07,129 --> 00:33:10,230
And in truth, it appeared to me the only possible one.

515
00:33:11,230 --> 00:33:15,889
Satisfied I was not, but to please him, I endeavoured to appear so.

516
00:33:16,790 --> 00:33:18,709
Relieved, I certainly did feel.

517
00:33:19,449 --> 00:33:21,589
So I answered him with a contented smile.

518
00:33:22,489 --> 00:33:27,050
And now, as it was long past one, I prepared to leave him.

519
00:33:28,489 --> 00:33:30,790
Does not Sophie sleep with Adele in the nursery?

520
00:33:31,489 --> 00:33:33,190
He asked, as I lit my candle.

521
00:33:34,589 --> 00:33:35,589
Yes, sir.

522
00:33:36,489 --> 00:33:40,309
And there is room enough in Adele's little bed for you.

523
00:33:41,309 --> 00:33:43,309
You must share it with her tonight, Jane.

524
00:33:44,290 --> 00:33:48,150
It is no wonder that the incident you have related should make you nervous,

525
00:33:48,690 --> 00:33:51,230
and I would rather you did not sleep alone.

526
00:33:52,430 --> 00:33:54,489
Promise me to go to the nursery.

527
00:33:55,889 --> 00:33:58,269
I shall be very glad to do so, sir.

528
00:33:59,389 --> 00:34:01,989
And fasten the door securely on the inside.

529
00:34:03,510 --> 00:34:08,449
Wake Sophie when you go upstairs, under pretence of requesting her to rouse

530
00:34:08,451 --> 00:34:10,913
you in good time tomorrow, for you must be

531
00:34:10,913 --> 00:34:14,891
dressed and have finished breakfast before eight.

532
00:34:17,750 --> 00:34:25,750
And now, no more soft whispers the wind has fallen.

533
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:30,370
And there is no more beating of rain against the window-pains.

534
00:34:31,230 --> 00:34:33,370
Look here, he lifted up the curtain.

535
00:34:34,069 --> 00:34:35,330
It is a lovely night.

536
00:34:36,569 --> 00:34:37,569
It was.

537
00:34:38,209 --> 00:34:40,370
Half heaven was pure and stainless.

538
00:34:41,349 --> 00:34:45,470
The clouds, now trooping before the wind, which had shifted to the west,

539
00:34:45,970 --> 00:34:48,470
were filing off eastward in long silvered columns.

540
00:34:49,449 --> 00:34:50,550
The moon shone peacefully.

541
00:34:52,949 --> 00:35:00,290
Well, said Mr. Rochester, gazing inquiringly into my eyes, how is my Janet now?

542
00:35:01,349 --> 00:35:03,629
The night is serene, sir, and so am I.

543
00:35:05,029 --> 00:35:07,959
And you will not dream of separation and sorrow

544
00:35:07,959 --> 00:35:11,069
tonight, but of happy love and blissful union.

545
00:35:12,550 --> 00:35:14,790
This prediction was but half fulfilled.

546
00:35:15,790 --> 00:35:19,529
I did not indeed dream of sorrow, but as little did I dream of joy,

547
00:35:20,069 --> 00:35:21,529
for I never slept at all.

548
00:35:22,470 --> 00:35:27,910
With little Adele in my arms, I watched the slumber of childhood, so tranquil,

549
00:35:28,230 --> 00:35:32,129
so passionless, so innocent, and waited for the coming day.

550
00:35:32,930 --> 00:35:35,389
All my life was awake and a stir in my frame.

551
00:35:36,410 --> 00:35:39,290
And as soon as the sun rose, I rose too.

552
00:35:40,730 --> 00:35:43,569
I remember Adele clung to me as I left her.

553
00:35:43,571 --> 00:35:48,989
I remember I kissed her as I loosened her little hands from my neck, and I cried

554
00:35:48,991 --> 00:35:53,089
over her with strange emotion, and quitted her because

555
00:35:53,091 --> 00:35:56,870
I feared my sobs would break her still sound repose.

556
00:35:57,809 --> 00:36:04,949
She seemed the emblem of my past life, and he, I was now to array myself to meet,

557
00:36:05,849 --> 00:36:10,410
the dread but a doored, type of my unknown future day.
